   "user": "How long do I have to report a problem with TXN-002411, and how long does the bank then have to investigate?",
   "answer": "You have two relevant time‑frames:\n\n**1. How long you have to report the problem**  \n*Regulation E* requires that a notice of error be received **no later than 60 days after the statement (or the electronic account history) that first shows the error**【1005.11(b)#1】. Northwind Bank’s own policy for this particular charge adds a stricter deadline: you must report the error **within 3 days** of the transaction, otherwise the claim is void【TXN‑002411 memo】.\n\n**2. How long the bank has to investigate**  \nOnce a valid notice is received, the bank must:\n\n* **Investigate and determine whether an error occurred within 10 business days** of receiving the notice【1005.11(c)#1】.  \n* If the investigation cannot be completed in that time, the bank may take **up to 45 days** (still from the date it received the notice) to finish the investigation, provided it provisionally credits your account within the first 10 business days【1005.11(c)#2】.  \n\nSo, for TXN‑002411 you should let us know **within 3 days** (bank policy) and, at the latest, **within 60 days** under Regulation E. After we receive your notice, we will investigate **within 10 business days**, or **up to 45 days** if more time is needed.",
